2026-09-26 17:56 Reproduced (git 2.47.3, real git, not constructed): builtin/reset.c order is checkout (unpack_trees) -> write index -> ORIG_HEAD -> HEAD. (1) A held branch ref lock makes reset --hard B fail at the ref update: checkout+index at B, HEAD at A, rev-parse --short HEAD = A. (2) A checkout write failing midway: a.txt already B, old.txt already deleted, index+HEAD at A. A SIGKILL leaves the same states (plus index.lock in (2)). Also found: reset --hard never removes untracked/ignored files, so a killed reset's new file (skills/new/SKILL.md) survives the NEXT ONLINE reset --hard to a commit without it (k84's 'restores exactly' holds only for tracked files) - git clean -ffdx removes it. Plan: fallback checks git status --porcelain --ignored -uall (GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0, no writes) and only when dirty runs reset --hard HEAD + clean -ffdx; a restore failure rejects the cache; online path adds clean -ffdx after its reset; repair() reads url+fetch in one config call and sets the default refspec when missing.

2026-09-26 18:03 Design: fallback = version() (commit/pin check) then restore(): git status --porcelain --ignored -unormal with GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0 (clean: ~3 ms, no write); dirty or status failing -> reset --hard HEAD + clean -ffdxq; failure (e.g. the killed run's fresh index.lock, < sweep age) -> CacheRejected, named as 'cache rejected (...)', source keeps its items. Chose check-first over always-reset: 1 process and no write vs 2 processes writing index/ORIG_HEAD/reflog each offline sync. Online: clean -ffdxq after reset (~2 ms vs the fetch). repair(): one 'config -z --get-regexp ^remote\.origin\.(url|fetch)$' read, sets +refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/* when fetch is missing. PinMismatch renamed CacheRejected. Behaviour change to flag: within 5 min of a kill mid-checkout, a source now errors (items kept) instead of installing the half-updated tree. No Changes file exists in the repo.

